<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>The fire insurance adjuster your insurer sends works for the insurer. A licensed public adjuster works for you.</li>
<li>Fire claims usually reach well beyond the burned area: smoke, soot, heat, and firefighting water travel through the building and HVAC system.</li>
<li>Fire is covered under your homeowners or commercial policy, not TWIA, which covers wind and hail only.</li>
<li>Texas prompt-payment rules give insurers set deadlines, extended to 30 days to decide if arson is suspected.</li>
